# Python. No trailing slash on .venv: a worktree is given a symlink to the one
# here rather than a copy of its own, and a directory pattern does not match a
# symlink - which left every worktree reporting an untracked file it did not
# create, and made "is anything uncommitted here?" a question with no answer.
.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Where lock-deps.sh keeps the pinned uv it resolves the locks with. Its own
# venv on purpose, so the resolver never becomes one of the things resolved.
.lockgen/

# 31 MB of wheels that fetch-wheels.sh downloads from the locks and release.yml
# rebuilds on every tag. The locks name and hash every one of them, so the
# files themselves carry nothing the repository does not already record.
wheels/

# Node and the built SPA. dist/ is a release artifact: install-panel.sh uses it
# when present, and the CI job publishes it, but it is never committed.
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Runtime state. On a server these live in /var/lib/awg-panel; here they are
# whatever `make dev` and `make test` left behind.
db.sqlite3
staticfiles/
.dev/
# `make demo` deletes this on the way out and again on the way in, so it should
# never be here to ignore. Listed for the run that was killed with -9, or that
# went down with the machine.
.demo/
